            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to have doubts, then the German for to doubt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: die Vermutung",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Vermutung — \"the guess, the supposition\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Meine Vermutung war richtig: Er hatte den Schlüssel im Auto vergessen. My guess was right: he had left the key in the car."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Vermutungen. The noun of vermuten."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Vermutung is the noun of vermuten \"to suppose\", which is usually traced to muten, from Mut in its old sense \"mind, feeling\". EtymDB has no entry for the verb, so the account is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
