          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: die Annahme",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Annahme — \"the assumption; the acceptance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Wir sind von der falschen Annahme ausgegangen, dass das Museum montags offen ist. We started from the wrong assumption that the museum is open on Mondays."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Annahmen. The noun of annehmen: die Annahme eines Pakets — accepting a parcel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Annahme is the noun of annehmen, built on nehmen \"to take\", inherited from Old High German neman and Proto-Germanic nemaną (EtymDB): something you take as given."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
