          "title": "You'll want to know: anscheinend",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "anscheinend — \"apparently, it seems\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Anscheinend ist niemand zu Hause: Alle Fenster sind dunkel. Apparently nobody is at home: all the windows are dark."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It says how things look, and they probably are so. Scheinbar says they only look so."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "anscheinend is the present participle of anscheinen \"to appear to\", built on scheinen \"to shine, to seem\", inherited from Old High German skīnan and Proto-Germanic skīnaną (EtymDB), a cousin of English shine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
